title: Keep chain-selection notified when a coalesced approval is only partly valid

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      `import_approval` processes every candidate named in a coalesced
      `ImportApproval` in one loop, writing overlay state and accumulating
      actions as it goes. A later per-candidate failure (typically
      `NoAssignment`) used to `respond_early!` with an empty action list,
      discarding `Action::NoteApprovedInChainSelection` even though the
      overlay already marked the block fully approved.

      There is no retry: a later remote approval or wakeup for an already
      approved candidate returns without re-emitting the notification, so
      chain-selection can treat a valid fork as unapproved until it goes
      stagnant.

      Per-candidate errors now skip that candidate and continue. Accumulated
      actions are always returned. The overall result remains `Bad` if any
      named candidate failed.

  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      Fixes a rare approval-voting liveness bug where a coalesced approval
      vote that mixed assigned and unassigned candidates could approve a
      block on disk without telling chain-selection. No CLI, config, or
      migration changes. Restart onto this binary to pick up the fix.

crates:
  - name: polkadot-node-core-approval-voting
    bump: patch
